      endTime: "19:00",
      tags: ["relational practice","human-centered design","storytelling","workforce"],
      description: "Storytelling must be a cornerstone of child welfare work driven by relationship, human connection, genuine empathy and sought understanding.   What if those who serve families in the child welfare system and who come into this work driven by genuine compassion to support and help heal were honored from day one of their employment in a way that allowed them, inspired them, encouraged them and enabled them to serve families and children well.  What if administrative demands, broken practices, unchecked biases, antiquated policies didn't interrupt the relational power of this work?  Learn what can happen if stories of those caught in this system that can have the tendency to silence them are actually heard and used to drive transformation.",
