      description: "This interactive panel brings forward the voices of young people who have grown up in child care institutions and are now stepping into adulthood. While much of today’s conversation about the future workforce focuses on technology, AI, and vocational skills, this session highlights something often overlooked: the power of empathy, emotional resilience, and community connection.Through storytelling, dialogue, and collaborative activities, participants will explore how current skilling systems miss the unique journeys of care-experienced youth. Together, we will map out ways to embed social-emotional learning, trauma-informed practices, and relational skills into education and workforce programs.A call to make skilling human-centered, inclusive, and empowering for every young person.",
