        { name: "Kristine Creavey", title: "Senior Researcher", org: "Chapin Hall", bio: "Kristine Creavey is a researcher at Chapin Hall at the University of Chicago, where she focuses on child welfare practice, implementation, and system improvement. Her work centers on strengthening decision-making processes, supporting frontline practice, and translating research into practical tools for agencies.She partners with public sector organizations to design and evaluate strategies aimed at improving outcomes for children and families, with an emphasis on applying evidence in real-world child welfare settings." },
        { name: "Tracy Rohrdanz", title: "Director of Customer Impact", org: "", bio: "Former caseworker turned technology leader dedicated to improving how child welfare work gets done. At Augintel, focuses on helping organizations turn complex narrative data into clear, actionable insight.Believes the people doing this work deserve better tools that reduce burden, strengthen decision making, and truly support the reality of frontline practice." }
